EuroGoTV1 [-\]\: Some information about the players\: Peter Brouwer is a strong 5d (I believe he will be promoted to 6d after this Championship). His nickname on kgs is Danoontje.
EuroGoTV1 [-\]\:  Gilles van Eeden is a Dutch 6d that has done very well in the past, but he has been inactive in the Dutch go world for about 20 years. He suddenly reappeared a couple of months ago and swiped the preliminaries for the Dutch Championships with 8 wins out of 8 games.
EuroGoTV1 [-\]\: Another anecdote on van Eeden\: way way back he was playing a Dutch Championship (don't know what year exactly), in which he tied with Guo Juan 5p for the title. They played a play-off in which the score was 1-1. When the decisive game was to be played, van Eeden didn't show and lost the title to Guo Juan.
EuroGoTV2 [-\]\: thanks man!
EuroGoTV1 [-\]\: the last bit of the story, the not-showing-up part, is something I've heard about, I'm not entirely sure it matches with what really happened
EuroGoTV1 [-\]\: he did beat Guo Juan once in that play off though, so he was plenty strong
EuroGoTV1 [-\]\: you are welcome
murky [1d\]\: interesting
EuroGoTV1 [-\]\: EuroGoTV at your service, haha
